From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 15:12:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Skip the PC speaker while it is silent

The PC speaker mixer added silence to every sample of the stream when no
sound played, it returns at once instead.
---
 id_sd.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/id_sd.c b/id_sd.c
index 5ea7ec6..4ad0be6 100644
--- a/id_sd.c
+++ b/id_sd.c
@@ -238,6 +238,15 @@ static void SDL_PCMixCallback(void *udata, Uint8 *stream, int len)
     int i;
     int nsamples;
 
+    // Without a sound playing the stream is left as it is, silence for the
+    // PC speaker, instead of adding zero to every sample
+
+    if (!pcSound && current_freq == 0)
+    {
+        current_remaining = 0;
+        return;
+    }
+
     // Number of samples is quadrupled, because of 16-bit and stereo
 
     nsamples = len / 4;
